# DM26-0670

# infra/release-baseline.nuon
#
# Where the platform's version numbering starts: the version, and the commit it is attached to. Used until the first
# release tag (vX.Y.Z) exists; after that, the latest tag is the previous release. It is a file and not a tag because
# no release was ever made at this commit, and a tag would say one was. The commit is the parent of the first commit
# that used conventional commit messages (af152e6), so that commit and everything after it counts toward the next version.
{
  version: "0.1.0"
  commit: "8dd4ca6133abac9c65181aeab61cc18d9efdbde0"
}
